From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] notifications: no calendar or contacts query where there is no
 provider

This device has neither a calendar nor a contacts provider, and nothing to put
in them: it has no accounts and no telephony. Two places asked anyway, and
every attempt logged an error of its own ("Failed to find provider info for
com.android.calendar", 8 lines, and the same for com.android.contacts, 7, in
one session of PW3 Android Test V48):

 - the zen-mode event rule's CalendarTracker, which the default rule set
   creates on every boot, and
 - SystemUI's user info, which reads the display name of the local profile on
   a single-user device.

Both now look the provider up first and skip the query when it is not
installed. A device that has the providers is unchanged.

--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/policy/UserInfoControllerImpl.java
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/policy/UserInfoControllerImpl.java
@@ -160,7 +160,10 @@
 
